/**

@mainpage Sofia-SIP su-cdlib Module [TODO!!]

@section su_cdlib_meta Module Meta Information

The su-cdlib module provides an interface to connect Sofia-SIP event loop
to an existing CDLib IOReactor based main loop. Without this interface, a
CDLib based application would have to create a separate thread for running
the Sofia-SIP event loop. The application using this module MUST call
IOReactor::create() before initializing the Sofia-SIP library and SHOULD
call IOReactor::destroy() when finished (su-cdlib always assumes IOReactor
singleton exists).

@CONTACT Tarik Miller <tmiller@slacorp.com>

@STATUS Core library

@LICENSE LGPL

@section su_cdlib_contents Contents of su-cdlib Module

The su-cdlib module contains the public header files as follows:
- <su_cdlib.h>    the public API of the module

@section su_cdlib_examples Examples of use

Below is a simple example of how to use su-cdlib:
@code
  #include <IOReactor.h>
  #include <BaseApplication.h>

extern "C"
{
  #include <sofia-sip/su_cdlib.h>
}

  class MyApp: public BaseApplication
  {
     /* ... */
  };

  /* ... */

  /* CDLib app context */
  MyApp myapp;

  /* create reactor singleton */
  IOReactor::create(1);

  /* create a sofia event loop using su-cdlib module */
  su_root_t *sofia_event_loop = su_cdlib_root_create(NULL);

  /* run the cdlib main loop */
  myapp.start(1);

  /* cleanup sofia event loop */
  su_root_destroy(sofia_event_loop);

  /* release reactor singleton when cleaning up */
  IOReactor::destroy();
  /* ... app shutdown/exit */
@endcode

@section su_cdlib_todo Todo

- docs.
